Third-party components
----------------------

Linked libraries (AGPL-3.0-only):
  - libsignal              https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal
    Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC. Some tests reproduce values from its
    own tests (backup credential presentations, key transparency wire
    formats) to check this app against it.
  - RingRTC (calls)        https://github.com/signalapp/ringrtc
    Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC.

Modified libraries, vendored in vendor/ (AGPL-3.0-only):
  - presage                https://github.com/whisperfish/presage
  - libsignal-service-rs   https://github.com/whisperfish/libsignal-service-rs
  Both are Copyright their upstream authors (the whisperfish contributors)
  and keep their licenses in vendor/*/LICENSE.md. They are modified
  versions, changed by Ken Powers for signal-gpui since 2026-10-15:
  vendor/README.md lists each change, and the git history of vendor/ dates
  it.

Signal Desktop (AGPL-3.0-only), Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC,
https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop:
  - Much of this app's behavior follows Signal Desktop, and parts of its
    logic are adapted from Desktop's TypeScript source (for example name
    formatting, the "Read more" cut, the story text color slider, poll
    limits, and retry back-off schedules). Code comments name the Desktop
    file each part follows.
  - Much of the English interface text (dialogs, notices, toasts, menu
    items) is taken from Signal Desktop's _locales/en/messages.json.
  - Icons, the ringtone and the app icon's logo, listed below.

Calls use WebRTC (BSD-3-Clause), Copyright (c) 2011, The WebRTC project
authors, linked from Signal's prebuilt library through RingRTC. Its license
and the licenses of the libraries it includes ship with that library, in
LICENSE.md next to libwebrtc.a (target/webrtc/release after a build).
Camera capture uses nokhwa (Apache-2.0).

